{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Cursed be their anger, for it was fierce.</b> Either by way of prophecy or by way of prayer — that their anger be diminished, and it be good for them. For 'cursed' is the opposite of 'blessed': just as blessing adds, so cursing subtracts." "<b>I will divide them.</b> The meaning is doubled, and likewise 'I will scatter them.' The meaning is that they are fit to be separated and not joined together. Now we have found that the lot of Simeon fell within the inheritance of the tribe of Judah, and it is under another's authority. And his cities too were not contiguous, but scattered throughout the lot of Judah. Likewise Levi, who had forty-eight cities — and they are scattered among the tribes."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:21.614077052Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}